```
public class PigLatinConverter {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String sentence = "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog";
        String[] words = sentence.split("\\s+");
        String pigLatinSentence = "";
        for (String word : words) {
            String pigLatinWord = convertToPigLatin(word);
            pigLatinSentence += pigLatinWord + " ";
        }
        System.out.println(pigLatinSentence.trim());
    }

    public static String convertToPigLatin(String word) {
        String firstLetter = word.substring(0, 1);
        String restOfWord = word.substring(1);
        String vowels = "AEIOUaeiou";
        String punctuation = ",.;:?!";
        String pigLatinWord = "";
        if (vowels.contains(firstLetter)) {
            pigLatinWord = word + "ay";
        } else {
            pigLatinWord = restOfWord + firstLetter + "ay";
        }
        if (Character.isUpperCase(firstLetter.charAt(0))) {
            pigLatinWord = pigLatinWord.substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + pigLatinWord.substring(1).toLowerCase();
        }
        if (punctuation.contains(restOfWord.substring(restOfWord.length() - 1))) {
            pigLatinWord = pigLatinWord.substring(0, pigLatinWord.length() - 2) + restOfWord.substring(restOfWord.length() - 1);
        }
        return pigLatinWord;
    }
}
```
Here's how the code works:
1. The `main` method initializes a sample sentence and splits it into an array of words using the `split` method.
2. It then loops through each word in the array and calls the `convertToPigLatin` method to convert it to piglatin.
3. The `convertToPigLatin` method takes a word as input and checks if its first letter is a vowel or consonant.
4. If the first letter is a vowel, it simply appends "ay" to the end of the word.
5. If the first letter is a consonant, it moves the consonant to the end of the word and appends "ay".
6. If the original word was capitalized, the piglatin word will also be capitalized.
7. If the original word ended with punctuation, the punctuation is preserved in the piglatin word.
