How can I create a program in Swift to solve the Mayan temple puzzle? 
I want to represent the levers as variables and their connections as a graph. Each lever will have an associated value representing the god it represents and its importance in Mayan mythology. 
To solve the puzzle, I will use a recursive function that takes in the current lever being pulled and its connections. The function will check if the lever being pulled is the correct one based on the order of importance of the gods. If it is, the function will move on to the next lever in the correct order. If not, it will try the next connected lever. 
Here's some sample code to get started:
```
struct Lever {
  let god: String
  let importance: Int
  var isConnectedTo: [Lever]
}
let jaguarLever = Lever(god: "jaguar", importance: 1, isConnectedTo: [featheredSerpentLever])
let featheredSerpentLever = Lever(god: "feathered serpent", importance: 2, isConnectedTo: [skullLever, sunLever])
let skullLever = Lever(god: "skull", importance: 3, isConnectedTo: [maizePlantLever])
let sunLever = Lever(god: "sun", importance: 4, isConnectedTo: [])
let maizePlantLever = Lever(god: "maize plant", importance: 5, isConnectedTo: [])
func solvePuzzle(currentLever: Lever, pulledLevers: [Lever]) -> Bool {
  // Check if all levers have been pulled in the correct order
  if pulledLevers.count == 5 {
    return true
  }

  // Try pulling each connected lever
  for connectedLever in currentLever.isConnectedTo {
    if !pulledLevers.contains(connectedLever) {
      var newPulledLevers = pulledLevers
      newPulledLevers.append(connectedLever)

      if solvePuzzle(currentLever: connectedLever, pulledLevers: newPulledLevers) {
        return true
      }
    }
  }

  return false
}
// Call the solvePuzzle function with the first lever (jaguar)
if solvePuzzle(currentLever: jaguarLever, pulledLevers: [jaguarLever]) {
  print("You have solved the Mayan temple puzzle!")
} else {
  print("Sorry, you were not able to solve the puzzle.")
}
